+# BLUE CURRENT V49.25.0 — LAUNCH STABILIZATION
+
+V49.21–V49.25 adds the post-launch stabilization layer between a human-recorded cutover and a location being declared operationally stable.
+
+## Stabilization observation
+
+A location enters stabilization only after a cutover result has been recorded.
+
+Each observation captures:
+
+- observation window
+- first-service verification
+- API health
+- authentication health
+- reservation integrity
+- floor integrity
+- kitchen integrity
+- workforce integrity
+- severity
+- incident/degradation description
+- operator note
+- timestamp / actor
+
+High or Critical severity requires an incident description.
+
+## Stabilization exit criteria
+
+Blue Current evaluates:
+
+1. Human-recorded cutover succeeded.
+2. At least one post-launch observation exists.
+3. First service is verified.
+4. Latest observation passes all health checks.
+5. No critical launch observation exists.
+6. Current leadership attention is not High/Critical.
+7. At least one clean first-service stabilization observation exists.
+
+## Rollback signal
+
+Blue Current surfaces `REVIEW_ROLLBACK` when launch evidence warrants leadership review, including:
+
+- cutover did not succeed
+- critical stabilization observation
+- repeated health failures
+- current High/Critical leadership attention
+
+This signal is advisory only.
+
+## Human stabilization declaration
+
+Adds:
+
+`POST /api/launch-stabilization/locations/:locationId/declare`
+
+Supported human decisions:
+
+- `STABLE`
+- `EXTEND`
+- `ROLLBACK`
+
+STABLE with open exit criteria requires a documented executive reason.
+
+ROLLBACK always requires a documented human reason.
+
+A rollback decision is stored as:
+
+- `decision: ROLLBACK`
+- `executionState: ROLLBACK_DECIDED_NOT_EXECUTED`
+
+Blue Current does not execute rollback.
+
+## API
+
+GET `/api/launch-stabilization`
+
+POST `/api/launch-stabilization/locations/:locationId/observe`
+
+POST `/api/launch-stabilization/locations/:locationId/declare`
+
+Observations require write/admin permission.
+
+Stabilization declarations require admin permission.
+
+## Safety policy
+
+- `observationIsHumanRecorded: true`
+- `rollbackRecommendationIsAdvisory: true`
+- `humanStabilizationDeclarationRequired: true`
+- `autonomousRollback: false`
+- `automaticStableDeclaration: false`
+
+## Current authenticated runtime
+
+The untouched Chefs runtime does not yet contain a successful human-recorded production cutover.
+
+V49.25 therefore correctly reports:
+
+- status: `successful-cutover-required`
+- locations in stabilization: 0
+- autonomous rollback: false
+- automatic stable declaration: false
+
+The current demo owner account is not an admin, and an attempted stabilization declaration correctly returns HTTP 403.
+
+## Focused lifecycle validation
+
+The focused lifecycle verifies:
+
+- successful cutover enters stabilization
+- clean first-service observation
+- six-of-six health confirmation
+- stabilization exit criteria pass
+- human STABLE declaration
+- critical launch degradation
+- rollback recommendation signal
+- ROLLBACK blocked without a reason
+- human ROLLBACK declaration
+- rollback remains NOT EXECUTED
+
+## Validation
+
+- V49.25 launch stabilization test PASS
+- V49.20 Go-Live Command regression PASS
+- authenticated launch-stabilization GET PASS
+- admin-only declaration boundary PASS
+- authoritative database unchanged
+- npm run check PASS
+- 896 JavaScript files
+- 756 client scripts
+- 5,645 unique HTML IDs
+
+## Next
+
+V49.26–V49.30 should close and certify V49:
+
+- complete V49 rollout chain certification
+- activation / technical / deployment / cutover / stabilization contract checks
+- authorization boundary regression
+- human-control safety audit
+- database write-integrity audit
+- startup/module/UI regression
+- stale/dead V49 surface review
+- final V49 release certification
